A||||5||Doni Hagan||LUBE ACCELERATOR CABLE?||||1||
Z||000000||Doni Hagan||08-06-2001||07:32 PM||||Is it possible to lube an accelerator cable? Mine seems to drag on occasion and I've had to pull the pedal up with my foot. Is it possible there could be a bend somewhere that's causing resistance? I've lubed all throttle linkages. Still happens. <P>Any thoughts? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||08-06-2001||07:52 PM||||Usually if that's happening and you already lubed it then the cable is failing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||08-06-2001||07:54 PM||||Thats how I wrecked my 86 coupe- the throttle cable would stick, I'd have to stick my foot under the gas pedal to get it working right. Ran smack into a Chevy Blazer when my foot got caught under the gas pedal, couldn't quite get to the brakes fast enough.<P>Replace the cable.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||08-06-2001||08:24 PM||||I tried lubing the cable on mine last fall. Made no difference. I decided to replace the cable(which was a major PITA), but throttle was nice and light feeling, plus I got rid of all the "power-robbing" slack, made a big difference in performance being able to fully open the throttle again.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Doni Hagan||08-09-2001||11:50 PM||||Okay...<P>So what you folks are saying is I have to replace the darn thing. Phooey! I replaced the accelerator pedal and THAT was a PITA!!<BR>I can just imagine what the cable replacement is like. <P>Oh, well...Once more into the breach.||||reg||9
Z||000005||Fiero*101||08-10-2001||01:30 AM||||Hey dont feel bad Doni  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>My 86 SE 2M6 is doing the same thing. But mine is not sticking its just when i put the pedal down it takes for ever for it to go.<P>The guy that sold it to me told me that its streched and its easy to fix. <P>but i just need the time and money to do it now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Fiero*101||||reg||1
